Parity scope reproduced from the web source:
  • Cron expression Input (placeholder "*/5 * * * *"), 5 preset chips
    (Every Minute/Hour/Day/Week/Month → exact web cron values), plain-English
    description, and the next-5 run timestamps.
  • describeCron + getNextCronRuns ported with byte-for-byte VALUE parity
    (the deliberately-loose web matcher semantics incl. NaN-as-no-match and the
    "ignore the token before /" behaviour are reproduced verbatim).
  • States: empty (guidance hint) · invalid<>5 fields (hint) · content
    (description + runs, with an empty-state row for a valid-but-impossible
    schedule). Every state renders — no blank box.
  • i18n: ALL web t() keys + the describeCron fragments / weekday names (web
    hardcodes the latter in helpers.ts) resolve through the per-surface P1/S10
    facade with byte-identical English fallbacks; zero hardcoded literals in code.
  • a11y: field label/value, per-preset labels, description + per-run VoiceOver
    labels, decorative glyphs hidden. Telemetry: view.opened slug "CronParser".
  • SwiftUI-free adapter/model (Foundation/Observation/OSLog); shared P1/S9 tokens
    + shared components (TSGlassPanel/TSButton/TSBadge); no ported Tailwind.

Flat-module note: my parser type was renamed CronExpression → CronParserExpression
to avoid a collision with the pre-existing TriggerConfigurator.CronExpression, per
the repo's established cross-surface dedupe practice (baseline commit b242fc213).

